=== layout: one-panel

# Read an Address

@body

A gene has a chromosome address, like a book has a library address.

{table-style=comparison text-align=left}
| Part | What It Names | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chromosome | Which chromosome? | 7 |
| Arm | Short p or long q? | q |
| Region | Which region of that arm? | 3 |
| Band | Which band in that region? | 1 |
| Subband | Which part of that band? | .2 |

=== layout: two-panels

# Try It: The CFTR Address

@left

*CFTR*: *7q31.2*

- Which chromosome?
- Which arm?
- Which region?
- Which band?
- Which subband?

